  {
    "index": 43,
    "sentence": "We wish to evaluate",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 44,
    "sentence": "S = ∑ₙ₌₁∞ [n/(n⁴ + 4)].",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 45,
    "sentence": "Step 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 46,
    "sentence": "Factor the Denominator",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 47,
    "sentence": "Notice that the quartic in the denominator factors nicely:\n  n⁴ + 4 = (n² - 2n + 2)(n² + 2n + 2).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 48,
    "sentence": "Step 2.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 49,
    "sentence": "Partial Fractions",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 50,
    "sentence": "We express the general term as a sum of two simpler fractions:\n  n/(n⁴ + 4) = n/[(n² - 2n + 2)(n² + 2n + 2)]\n       = [A·n + B] / (n² - 2n + 2) + [C·n + D] / (n² + 2n + 2).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 51,
    "sentence": "Multiply both sides by (n² - 2n + 2)(n² + 2n + 2) to get:\n  n = (A·n + B)(n² + 2n + 2) + (C·n + D)(n² - 2n + 2).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 52,
    "sentence": "Expanding both products:\n  (A·n + B)(n² + 2n + 2) = A·n³ + 2A·n² + 2A·n + B·n² + 2B·n + 2B,\n  (C·n + D)(n² - 2n + 2) = C·n³ - 2C·n² + 2C·n + D·n² - 2D·n + 2D.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 53,
    "sentence": "Combine like terms:\n  n³:  A + C,\n  n²:  2A + B - 2C + D,\n  n¹:  2A + 2B + 2C - 2D,\n  constant: 2B + 2D.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 54,
    "sentence": "Since the left side is just n, we equate coefficients:\n  Coefficient of n³: A + C = 0           (1)\n  Coefficient of n²: 2A + B - 2C + D = 0      (2)\n  Coefficient of n¹: 2A + 2B + 2C - 2D = 1     (3)\n  Constant term:  2B + 2D = 0           (4)",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 55,
    "sentence": "From (1): C = -A.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 56,
    "sentence": "From (4): B + D = 0 ⟹ D = -B.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 57,
    "sentence": "Substitute C = -A and D = -B into (2):\n  2A + B - 2(-A) - B = 2A + B + 2A - B = 4A = 0 ⟹ A = 0.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 58,
    "sentence": "Thus, C = 0.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 59,
    "sentence": "Now substitute A = 0, C = 0, and D = -B into (3):\n  0 + 2B + 0 - 2(-B) = 2B + 2B = 4B = 1 ⟹ B = 1/4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 60,
    "sentence": "Then, D = -1/4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 61,
    "sentence": "So the partial fractions decomposition is:\n  n/(n⁴ + 4) = (1/4)/(n² - 2n + 2) - (1/4)/(n² + 2n + 2).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 62,
    "sentence": "Step 3.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 63,
    "sentence": "Rewrite in a Telescoping Form",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 64,
    "sentence": "Notice that:\n  n² - 2n + 2 = (n - 1)² + 1  and  n² + 2n + 2 = (n + 1)² + 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 65,
    "sentence": "Thus, we can write:\n  S = (1/4) ∑ₙ₌₁∞ [1/((n - 1)² + 1) - 1/((n + 1)² + 1)].",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 66,
    "sentence": "Now, split the sum into two parts:\n  S = (1/4) { ∑ₙ₌₁∞ 1/((n - 1)² + 1) - ∑ₙ₌₁∞ 1/((n + 1)² + 1) }.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 67,
    "sentence": "Re-index the sums:\n• For the first sum, let m = n - 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 68,
    "sentence": "Then when n = 1, m = 0 and as n → ∞, m → ∞.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 69,
    "sentence": "So:\n  ∑ₙ₌₁∞ 1/((n - 1)² + 1) = ∑ₘ₌₀∞ 1/(m² + 1).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 70,
    "sentence": "• For the second sum, let k = n + 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 71,
    "sentence": "Then when n = 1, k = 2 and as n → ∞, k → ∞.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 72,
    "sentence": "So:\n  ∑ₙ₌₁∞ 1/((n + 1)² + 1) = ∑ₖ₌₂∞ 1/(k² + 1).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 73,
    "sentence": "Thus,\n  S = (1/4) { [∑ₘ₌₀∞ 1/(m² + 1)] - [∑ₖ₌₂∞ 1/(k² + 1)] }.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 74,
    "sentence": "Notice that the difference of these two sums leaves only the m = 0 and m = 1 terms:\n  ∑ₘ₌₀∞ 1/(m² + 1) - ∑ₖ₌₂∞ 1/(k² + 1) = 1/(0² + 1) + 1/(1² + 1) = 1 + 1/2 = 3/2.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 75,
    "sentence": "Step 4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 76,
    "sentence": "Final Answer",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 77,
    "sentence": "Thus, the sum is:\n  S = (1/4) · (3/2) = 3/8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Answer"
  },
  {
    "index": 78,
    "sentence": "So, the value of the infinite sum is 3/8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Answer"
  }
